    "answer": {
      "short": "$4\\text{ cm}$. Equate the areas: $200x^2=128(x+1)^2$ and take the positive solution.",
      "worked": "Let $x$ be the original tile side length in centimetres, with $x>0$. Both sets of tiles cover the same area.\n$$\\begin{align*}200x^2&=128(x+1)^2\\\\200x^2&=128x^2+256x+128\\\\72x^2-256x-128&=0\\\\9x^2-32x-16&=0\\end{align*}$$\nHere $a=9$, $b=-32$ and $c=-16$.\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=\\frac{-(-32)\\pm\\sqrt{(-32)^2-4(9)(-16)}}{2(9)}\\\\x&=\\frac{32\\pm\\sqrt{1600}}{18}\\\\x&=\\frac{32\\pm40}{18}\\\\x&=4\\text{ or }-\\frac49\\end{align*}$$\nReject $-\\frac49$ because a side length must be positive. Each original tile has side length $4\\text{ cm}$.\nCheck: $200(4)^2=3200\\text{ cm}^2$ and $128(5)^2=3200\\text{ cm}^2$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
